   "description": "Run status: confirmatory (all nine anatomies, one commit, declared settings); commits ae458a9. (a) g4_confirm_summary.json anatomy[<anatomy>].endpoint.s50_ratio_squid_over_opm (value, value_bounds, value_censored, ci95), dark, and results/g4/g4_pediatric_comparison.json comparison['<anatomy>/paired/opm_dense/opm_vs_squid/combined/practical@1/depth0'].s50_ratio_squid_over_opm, light (checked equal to anatomy[<anatomy>].exploratory). Text: locations_favouring_opm : locations_favouring_squid; Holm p from families['endpoint'].holm_p (dark) and anatomy[<anatomy>].exploratory.holm_p_over_present_anatomies (light). (b) anatomy[<anatomy>].oracle and (c) anatomy[<anatomy>].mismatch (.s50_ratio_squid_over_opm), with families['secondary/opm_dense/opm_vs_squid/combined/oracle/replicate0'] and ['.../mismatch@1/replicate0'].holm_p; grey bars: the endpoint's point estimate. A tick and bold: Holm-adjusted p below the declared alpha (0.05). Shared logarithmic x axis 0.7\u20132 (display choice: the drawn values and finite interval ends with a margin); open interval ends are arrows to the axis edge. Anatomies in the order of scripts/report_style.py ANAT_ORDER with its labels, classes separated by hairlines. Drawn as: value.",
   "alt": "Three forest plots of the S50 ratio Neuromag over OPM on a log axis with a line at 1, one row per anatomy (9). In the confirmatory run the dense array's ratio is 1.27\u20131.47, against 1.18\u20131.65 in the exploratory run; the declared test passes after Holm correction in 9 of 9 anatomies (Adult, School size, 2-y size, 24 mo, 18 mo, 12 mo, Child A, Child B, Child C), and the interval includes 1 for none. The oracle detector's ratio is 1.27\u20131.62 (Holm p below 0.05: Adult, School size, 2-y size, 24 mo, 18 mo, 12 mo, Child A, Child B, Child C); the mismatched detector's 1.23\u20131.50 (Holm p below 0.05: Adult, School size, 2-y size, 24 mo, 18 mo, 12 mo, Child A, Child B, Child C).",
   "caption_draft": "Figure R16. Confirmatory spike run. Strength for 50 % detection, Neuromag (306 channels) over the dense OPM array, for focal spikes 10\u201320 mm below the scalp, paired on identical simulated spikes at 36 newly drawn locations per anatomy (> 1: the OPM detects at a lower strength); lines: 95 % location-bootstrap intervals; arrows: open ends; open markers: censored estimates. (a) The endpoint declared before the run (practical scanning detector, thresholds frozen at 1 false event per minute, first noise realization): ratios 1.27\u20131.47; the two-sided location sign-flip test, Holm-adjusted over the anatomies, is below 0.05 in 9 of 9. Light: the exploratory run (18 locations per anatomy, endpoint chosen after the analyses), ratios 1.18\u20131.65. (b) Oracle detector (known topography, waveform and time): ratios 1.27\u20131.62. (c) Mismatched detector (templates between the simulated morphologies and candidate fields from a 1-layer model with a 2-mm / 2-deg coregistration error), thresholds recalibrated to the same rate: ratios 1.23\u20131.50. Panels (b) and (c) are secondary analyses, each Holm-adjusted within its own family; grey bars mark the endpoint's ratio. The adult at its measured head position, the other heads at top contact in the fixed adult helmet.",
